WEBVTT

00:00:00.059 --> 00:00:03.299
Contacts gives your department a shared directory of people,

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.309
organizations, and locations.

00:00:05.679 --> 00:00:09.960
Keep member accounts and roster roles in Personnel; use this directory

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.119
for useful operational references.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.630
In our fictional Chicago Fire training department, we are in

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.770
Contacts, on the Categories page.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.979
The category table separates its name, description, color, and contact count.

00:00:23.299 --> 00:00:26.110
It starts empty here, even though the department already

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:28.069
has uncategorized contacts.

00:00:28.379 --> 00:00:32.380
We will create a small partner directory and verify each saved entry.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:34.089
Choose Add Category.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:38.949
Enter Academy Partner Directory as the Name and describe it as fictional

00:00:38.949 --> 00:00:41.330
training partners and logistics contacts.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:44.849
Keep the blue color so the category is easy to recognize.

00:00:45.179 --> 00:00:49.369
Display On Map remains unchecked and Map Icon stays Default.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.469
Those controls are separate from organizing the directory.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:54.000
Save, then

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.560
read the returned category row.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.310
Its name, description, and blue color are present, while

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.439
Contacts In Category is zero.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.879
That saved row is our starting point for adding contacts.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:10.139
On the Add Contact form, select Person, then Academy Partner Directory.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.880
Enter Sylvie and Brett in the first and last name fields.

00:01:14.249 --> 00:01:18.520
The organization field can add context; here it contains Academy

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.670
Community Partners, marked fictional.

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:24.900
Email Address and Cell Phone hold deliberately reserved training values.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.349
Scroll to Description and explain the purpose of the entry.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.529
Our text identifies a fictional community partner liaison and

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.560
asks the reader to verify current details before operational use.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:39.450
Keep that description useful and specific.

00:01:39.629 --> 00:01:44.119
After saving the person, use the Contacts table Search field to enter Brett.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:48.950
The result shows Sylvie Brett, the Person type, and the named category.

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:51.000
Choose View and check the

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.049
saved name and training contact channels.

00:01:53.389 --> 00:01:55.870
Scroll down to read the complete Description again.

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:59.290
These separate checks confirm that both the identity and the

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:00.829
useful context were stored.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:05.419
To verify category membership, use the named category in the list or

00:02:05.419 --> 00:02:09.989
the edit form; the Additional Info category value on this View is numeric.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:13.230
Create a second entry using Location or Company.

00:02:13.659 --> 00:02:17.819
Keep the same category, leave the person name fields empty, and enter

00:02:17.849 --> 00:02:22.229
Academy Logistics Desk, marked fictional, in Company Location Name.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:26.000
The organization has its own reserved training email

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.059
and an Office Phone

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.030
ending in zero one four three.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.690
Its Description explains that it is a fictional supply and

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.620
mutual-aid coordination contact.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:38.120
Using the appropriate contact type and phone field makes the

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:41.680
directory easier to understand when someone else opens the entry.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:47.209
In Location Info, GPS Location has a latitude field and a longitude field.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.499
Enter the complete fictional Chicago pair together.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:55.560
Entrance GPS Location and Exit GPS Location are separate pairs

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.430
and stay blank in this exercise.

00:02:57.899 --> 00:03:01.919
Continue to Physical Address and enter the fictional Training Avenue street,

00:03:02.069 --> 00:03:04.159
Chicago, Illinois, and postal code.

00:03:04.639 --> 00:03:08.610
Check Same as Physical under Mailing Address, then use Save

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:09.799
at the bottom of the form.

00:03:10.309 --> 00:03:14.520
These are stored directory reference values; entering coordinates does not

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.920
establish a device position, a verified entrance, or a successful route.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:23.570
Back in Contacts, select Academy Partner Directory in the category tree.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:28.890
Both newly saved entries appear: the person and the logistics organization.

00:03:29.359 --> 00:03:31.489
Now enter Logistics in Search.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:36.410
The table narrows the selected category to the organization, and the count says that

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:38.919
one result is filtered from two entries.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:42.380
Read the name and type before choosing View or Edit.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:47.019
A short list can reflect the combination of these filters, so check the selected

00:03:47.019 --> 00:03:50.749
category and search text before deciding that an entry is missing.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.539
Open the saved organization.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:56.910
Contact Details shows its name and email, and Location Info

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:58.689
shows the stored coordinate pair.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:02.980
Farther down, verify the physical address and original Description.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.800
For the named category and copied mailing address, return

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.490
to the list and choose Edit.

00:04:08.929 --> 00:04:11.000
The category is selected by name,

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.580
and the reopened mailing fields contain the copied

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.269
street, city, state, and postal code.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.359
Same as Physical is clear on reopening here.

00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:23.710
Check those actual fields rather than assuming the blank mailing section on

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.749
View proves that nothing was saved.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:29.720
Use a small, easy-to-check edit to confirm your maintenance workflow.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:35.220
In the reopened organization form, Office Phone ends in zero one four three.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.550
Change that final digit to four.

00:04:37.949 --> 00:04:41.419
After saving and reopening the same contact, the field now

00:04:41.449 --> 00:04:43.389
ends in zero one four four.

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:47.040
Read the reopened value, not just the value you typed.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.880
The original supply and mutual-aid Description remains in place.

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:54.960
A successful change to one field is a reason to verify that field

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:58.670
specifically, rather than assume every attempted edit was stored.

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:00.389
Finish in Categories.

00:05:00.809 --> 00:05:04.140
Academy Partner Directory now contains two contacts.

00:05:04.539 --> 00:05:08.480
Give someone responsibility for reviewing those details as partners change.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:12.300
Chicago Fire can use this pattern for logistics contacts.

00:05:12.659 --> 00:05:16.400
Community care and mental health teams can maintain operational partner

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.410
directories without patient detail.

00:05:18.779 --> 00:05:23.330
Search and rescue can organize staging and support contacts; security teams

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:27.759
can group site contacts; wildland crews can maintain supply references;

00:05:28.009 --> 00:05:32.249
and industrial response teams can organize facility coordination contacts.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:36.830
In each setting, choose clear categories, verify saved values,

00:05:37.089 --> 00:05:38.710
and keep the directory current.

